{
 "subtitle": "The taste family on family/taste, with the plain baseline and the no-taste control of next-taste: 1.1M env steps each, size50m, scored on the same 30 fixed worlds with tools/death_eval.py. (M) = masked: the run uses the rule mask, which reads the game's action rules, so it counts as cheating. Updated 2026-11-08.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over 30 evaluation episodes, ± its standard error over those worlds; unlock rates are the share of episodes in which an achievement fired; return is the mean raw Craftax return as a % of the maximum (226). Every checkpoint is scored on the same fixed worlds (env.reseed, audit B05), so comparisons are paired world by world. The error bars cover the worlds only, not training seeds.\nTaste did not help anywhere it was tried. Over actions on plain DreamerV3 (abl_taste) it scores 4.63 against plain's 4.77 (-0.13 ± 0.27, paired). In place of v2's rule mask (v2_taste) it scores 5.33, above vanilla (+0.70 ± 0.28) and level with its no-taste control in training. On the manager of the next agent (next_taste, masked) it scores 9.80, against 11.20 for the same agent with taste switched off (next_lam0, masked); over 60 worlds 9.38 against 11.30, -1.92 ± 0.41.",
 "table_note": "ach. ± SE = mean episode-final achievements ± standard error over the 30 worlds (one training seed). w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. return = raw Craftax return, % of 226. Rates are % of episodes. Vanilla: the original checkpoint (code before the 2026-10 fixes), re-scored on the fixed worlds. Plain: main's code, --configs craftax size50m --env.craftax.survival none (seed 0). The taste runs were trained on the fixed code (abl_taste and next_taste on 49a6bc3, v2_taste on cbec67b); their exact flags are in README.md. (M) = masked: uses the rule mask, counted as cheating, so not comparable with the rest. Next, no taste is the no-taste control of next-taste (taste computed but lam_mgr 0); the run lives on family/next.",
